{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =6[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the missing entries are $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $r=6.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399489 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399490 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399491 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1080 #uuid "c9bcdf0a-7ee5-512b-8b69-1c9ff761e1cb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1081 "$\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1084 #uuid "d416963d-0812-5442-bfb3-5143f8304cd1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1081 "$\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ and $9$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1084 #uuid "25b68c79-4c84-5a8a-b3cb-c873ab4bbeec" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1081 "$\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ and $9$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1084 #uuid "399087ad-ae5c-50a9-b3f6-f634f021724e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1081 "$\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1084 #uuid "abe1e0eb-b3fa-5749-9d80-faecfb2587cc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1081 "$\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1084 #uuid "e4b9e256-2bbe-5a6c-804a-deec95112ee2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399495 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1069 "q-140449" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1072 #uuid "f772a19b-8ab2-5f26-9ef1-47231e01914d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399496 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399498 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1080 #uuid "8ed14d3f-a85e-59d0-a5e0-cd86b0195649" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,0,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1084 #uuid "7c340906-07d4-57b0-9046-295287f1840f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,4,9}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1084 #uuid "735c9554-2122-554a-9c6d-88f5c542af17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,-2,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1084 #uuid "cf676211-b439-541c-a870-387de50e341e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1084 #uuid "5f97e983-0e63-57dd-acda-842c7a7cfb12" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1081 "\\lambda \\in {-3,4,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1084 #uuid "812db70d-b4af-5153-8bf4-a315c5a42142" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399502 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1069 "q-140555" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-7\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1072 #uuid "e9992e79-a8b1-5b6c-bb33-ddbd38d4ce02" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variables ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1})+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}) & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}+4-4)+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}+1-1) & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}+2)^{2}+({x}_{2}-1)^{2}-4 & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}+2)^{2}+({x}_{2}-1)^{2} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+2, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich defines an empty set. Notice that the equation is equivalent to $\\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(2\\text{i})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})^{2}}=1,$ which has imaginary solutions, so we can interpret this as an imaginary ellipse with semiaxes $2\\text{i}$ and $\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399503 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399504 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399505 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399506 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399507 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399504 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1080 #uuid "8d7df124-dbc5-56d7-8581-3302e8d894bc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1084 #uuid "74b0f0ad-077e-5490-8903-2b75e6400fb3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1081 "An imaginary ellipse" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1084 #uuid "c9962984-13d2-5e7a-a101-99ffb98df884" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $4$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1084 #uuid "c26a296a-362d-571b-bc2a-b4d7be4f7f68" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1084 #uuid "5b9951ca-7918-51ae-8e54-71674985b355" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $4$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1084 #uuid "70050e40-2d4d-5f43-8504-d04583bd8a31" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399509 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1069 "q-140822" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1071 "Scientists are observing a colony of bugs. The population $P(t)$ of the colony is given by the function\n\n$$\nP(t)=27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ is the number of bugs, and $t>0$ is the time (in days) since the observation started. \n\nAt what time is the population of the colony a minimum, and what is the number of bugs at this time?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1072 #uuid "3cbfc231-381e-525d-b699-91d7448dd5be" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1074 "To find when the population is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0$ for $t>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 3({t}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =4 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=2.$\nTo find the number of bugs when $t=2,$ we figure out $P(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & =27+{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27+[{x}^{3}-12x]{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =27+[(8-24)-(0)] \\\\  & =27-16 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $11<27$, we conclude that the minimum population is $11$ bugs, and this happens after $2$ days." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399510 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399511 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399512 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399513 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399514 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399514 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1080 #uuid "5e151de4-60bd-5c74-b6e4-910b2f3a14f4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1081 "The minimum is $8$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1084 #uuid "abcdf400-bcb6-5e0b-9ec6-dab2bf54761d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1081 "The minimum is $27$ bugs after $5$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1084 #uuid "ab9c13c6-09fb-581a-8fa8-e20695647309" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1081 "The minimum is $15$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1084 #uuid "7235e376-c628-51f5-8028-177047d2588a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1081 "The minimum is $16$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1084 #uuid "5f2d7c8e-9f10-5045-82f9-c14578f74b9e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1081 "The minimum is $11$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1084 #uuid "6f60dfcf-9cc7-5683-856d-afa629682956" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399516 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1069 "q-140997" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1071 "Given the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2},$ find its canonical (diagonal) form ${y}^{T}\\,Dy$ and an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that $x=Py$ defines the corresponding change of variables." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1072 #uuid "2172cdc2-fb35-5393-84ba-3c3dbc3c7926" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1074 "First, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nEvery quadratic form can be reduced to its canonical (diagonal) form using orthogonal transformations.\n\nTo find the coefficients of the canonical form, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =6,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$ \n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-6I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-6I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-1I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]-1[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-1I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ (writing the eigenvalues in descending order) and the orthogonal matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399517 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399518 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399519 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399520 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399521 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399519 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1080 #uuid "b9d3fb41-4434-5c99-a083-41daf1b7f0a5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true]