ectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.5$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in {0,2,4},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=0) & =\\frac{f(0,0)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(0,2)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.5}=0.2 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399587 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399588 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399589 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399590 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399591 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399591 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399586 1080 #uuid "232c8a87-8c1b-58ee-be3e-6552e315bf0f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399587 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399587 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399587 1084 #uuid "24afd0b0-d6de-56bf-ae8f-4be3381c967b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399588 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.25$ | $